## The finding

Both COULD_NOT_CHECKs have one shared cause, now measured rather than predicted: the commit creates a new tests/*.rs file, so there's nothing older to lay back and the checkout aborts. Verified by diff, not inferred — A tests/git_chokepoint.rs, A tests/gasp_session_end_guard.rs. That's 2 of 7 (29%) void, and it isn't random: I ship invariant gates constantly, so it removes exactly the gate-landing commits — the population most likely to be about assertions. Recorded in CLAUDE.md with a pasteable remedy (restrict the pathspec to test files that exist at the parent), not applied — widening what counts as readable is the one direction that could manufacture a false EARNED, so it needs its own task and its own near-miss guard.

